cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenAcquis or its dataset, please cite it as below. The dataset is CC-BY-4.0; the code is MIT."
type: software
title: "OpenAcquis: open map of how EU directives are transposed into national law"
abstract: >-
  Provision-level map of how EU directives are written into national law: notified national measures,
  directive and national texts split into provisions with stable IDs, machine-suggested links with gap and
  extra-rule candidates for human review, and an open dataset of links from official correlation tables and
  human review. Machine suggestions are candidates, not findings about transposition.
authors:
  - family-names: Kraus
    given-names: Vojtech
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JerryWoof/OpenAcquis"
url: "https://jerrywoof.github.io/OpenAcquis/"
keywords:
  - EU law
  - transposition
  - EUR-Lex
  - legal informatics
  - open data
  - NIS2
